WEBVTT

00:03.920 --> 00:04.400
All right.

00:04.440 --> 00:05.680
Now the Or operator.

00:05.720 --> 00:08.680
It says at least one condition must be true.

00:08.680 --> 00:10.600
So it is less restrictive than the.

00:10.640 --> 00:12.760
And it is enough to have one condition.

00:12.760 --> 00:13.160
True.

00:13.200 --> 00:15.240
In order to keep the row in the results.

00:15.280 --> 00:17.000
Let's understand exactly what this means.

00:17.040 --> 00:18.640
Okay, so now we have the same scenario.

00:18.680 --> 00:19.960
We have two conditions.

00:19.960 --> 00:25.760
And in SQL you have to connect them either using the and operator or the or operator.

00:25.760 --> 00:28.200
And this scenario we're going to talk about the Or operator.

00:28.200 --> 00:33.840
And as we said at least one of the conditions must be fulfilled in order to leave the record in the

00:33.840 --> 00:34.320
results.

00:34.320 --> 00:35.880
So let's see what's going to happen here.

00:35.920 --> 00:42.200
Now the first customer, Maria, she is not fulfilling the first condition and as well the second condition.

00:42.200 --> 00:43.760
So both of them is false.

00:43.760 --> 00:49.520
And this is the only scenario where SQL cannot remove the record from the results because it is not

00:49.520 --> 00:50.760
fulfilling the minimum.

00:50.760 --> 00:52.400
At least one of them should be true.

00:52.440 --> 00:53.560
Both of them is false.

00:53.560 --> 00:55.520
Then SQL can go and remove this row.

00:55.560 --> 00:57.440
Now moving on to the next one to John.

00:57.640 --> 01:01.280
John is from USA and has higher score than 500.

01:01.320 --> 01:04.600
Both of the conditions is green, so both of them is true.

01:04.600 --> 01:08.000
And this is more than enough to keep the row in the output.

01:08.000 --> 01:09.800
That's why we will see John in the output.

01:09.840 --> 01:11.600
Now moving on to the third one George.

01:11.640 --> 01:16.080
George is not fulfilling the first condition because UK is not equal to USA.

01:16.240 --> 01:19.600
Adjourn this time is fulfilling the second condition.

01:19.600 --> 01:20.440
So we have here.

01:20.440 --> 01:20.920
True.

01:20.920 --> 01:25.880
And since we have at least one true, this is good enough to keep the record in the output.

01:25.880 --> 01:28.100
So you will see George in their results.

01:28.140 --> 01:29.500
Now moving on to Martin.

01:29.500 --> 01:34.020
He is not fulfilling the first condition as well, not fulfilling the second condition.

01:34.020 --> 01:35.180
Both of them is false.

01:35.180 --> 01:38.140
And this is not enough to keep their result in the output.

01:38.140 --> 01:39.980
So that's why SQL can go and remove it.

01:40.020 --> 01:41.780
Now moving on to the last one better.

01:41.780 --> 01:45.420
He is fulfilling the first condition but not the second condition.

01:45.420 --> 01:49.580
But still everything is fine because he is fulfilling at least one condition.

01:49.580 --> 01:52.580
So we have the minimum and the SQL going to leave it in the outputs.

01:52.580 --> 01:56.700
So as you can see, the Or operator is not restrictive like the and operator.

01:56.700 --> 02:00.020
It's enough to have one true in order to keep the data in the output.

02:00.020 --> 02:02.780
And this is exactly how the Or operator works.

02:02.820 --> 02:04.140
Now let's see the second task.

02:04.180 --> 02:10.180
Retrieve all customers who are either from USA or have a score greater than 500.

02:10.220 --> 02:11.860
So it is a very similar task.

02:11.860 --> 02:13.060
We have two conditions.

02:13.060 --> 02:16.020
So we need the customers that are either from USA.

02:16.140 --> 02:19.140
So it is based on this country equal to USA.

02:19.180 --> 02:22.980
And the second condition is the score is greater than 500.

02:23.020 --> 02:24.900
But this time we are very relaxed.

02:24.900 --> 02:27.660
Either this condition is fulfilled or the second one.

02:27.660 --> 02:31.260
So instead of having ands we will be using the operator or.

02:31.300 --> 02:33.980
So it is enough to fulfill one of those conditions.

02:33.980 --> 02:39.580
And if you go and execute now as you can see, we are getting more results because it is easier to fulfill

02:39.580 --> 02:40.340
the conditions.

02:40.340 --> 02:45.540
So we can see those three customers either fulfilling the first condition or the second one.

02:45.580 --> 02:46.380
All right, my friends.

02:46.380 --> 02:47.500
So that's all for the Or.

02:47.500 --> 02:51.020
Operator and we're going to move to the last one in this group, the nuts.

